    "blocks": [
      {
        "index": 0,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "[Original description"
      },
      {
        "index": 1,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "A small entrance leads to a climb down into a small chamber with a strong draught. When the entrance was photographed in the summer, 2012, no draught was noticed. The cave was surveyed in July 2024 with the draught shown."
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "The cave was extended for about 50m beyond the dig in December 2024. A small, 1m high, stream passage was followed to a \"sizeable chamber with a large flowstone dome.\" There are other possible routes to look at, and it is hoped to further document the extension at Easter 2025. ]"
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "Note: The length above is incorporated into the length of Risco, i.e. 11840 + 870m = 12710m (May 2026)"
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "Updated description after being extended and linked to Risco at the Tonto Series, April 2025: [Pete Smith]"
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "The continuation of the cave is through a low crawl at the bottom of the passage on the left of the entrance. It gradually increases in size, picks up a tiny stream, and soon comes to a chamber with a flowstone dome straight ahead. After crossing the flowstone, a scramble down drops into a larger passage. To the right in the chamber, the passage meets an inlet on the right and then continues to a more exposed climb down to the same large passage. Directly opposite this climb, a walking size inlet, the Philosopher's Stone , heads in a north-east direction for about 45m and then turns towards the south for a further 55m before ending in a choke."
      },
      {
        "index": 6,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "The main passage, Fool's Gold , continues mostly as a high and narrow rift passage with the stream. An unsurveyed inlet enters under the right-hand wall. After about 150m of walking and shuffling sideways, the stream cuts down and it's necessary to climb up a couple of metres to the continuation on a higher level. This comes to the top of an 11m pitch. There appears to be an alcove on the right across the pitch. It is impossible to see if a passage enters there and it can only be reached by traversing."
      },
      {
        "index": 7,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "The traverse was rigged in 2026. A bolted traverse (six bolts) leads to a calcited ledge and a junction. To the left, a meandering passage intersects the pitch rift before crossing to the opposite side. This passage continues, becoming smaller but remaining navigable, and requires further exploration ( West Passage ). The main passage continues across a false floor overhanging a pitch. This drop ( Doxi Pitch ) requires rigging for a safe descent and investigation. A climb through boulders ascends approximately 10m into a 15m long upper level. The route continues upward into the ceiling through further boulders and remains a promising lead for a future trip. [AI logbook interpretation]"
      },
      {
        "index": 8,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "The pitch drops in fact into the chamber that was reached at the end of the Tonto Series in the Risco System (# 0025 ) in 1975. The stream that has been followed in Fool's Gold is joined at the bottom of the pitch by another stream that emerges out of a tiny sump. The combined waters flow into the Tonto Series , which is described with the main Risco system."
      }
    ],
