o a calcited ledge and a junction. To the left, a meandering passage intersects the pitch rift before crossing to the opposite side. This passage continues, becoming smaller but remaining navigable, and requires further exploration ( West Passage ). The main passage continues across a false floor overhanging a pitch. This drop ( Doxi Pitch ) requires rigging for a safe descent and investigation. A climb through boulders ascends approximately 10m into a 15m long upper level. The route continues upward into the ceiling through further boulders and remains a promising lead for a future trip. [AI logbook interpretation]\n\nThe pitch drops in fact into the chamber that was reached at the end of the Tonto Series in the Risco System (# 0025 ) in 1975. The stream that has been followed in Fool's Gold is joined at the bottom of the pitch by another stream that emerges out of a tiny sump. The combined waters flow into the Tonto Series , which is described with the main Risco system."
